            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="LEN01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>John</forename>
                        <surname>Lens</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1756-01-02">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1825-08-06"/>
                    <occupation>serjeant-at-law</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Godwin records his death.  There are also two instances in the Diary where Godwin mentions writing to Lens.
    </p>
                        <p> These letters are not extant and cannot be proved to be the same
    person, but it does seem quite likely. Lens was a prominent lawyer, and 
    born in Norwich - where he would have been a contemporary of Godwin's
    (both b. 1756). Godwin may have been writing for professional 
    advice or more personal letters - the <title>DNB</title> says that Lens became
    seriously ill in 1823.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other">
                        <title>DNB</title>
                    </bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
